      "content": "It sounds like you’ve convinced yourself that disappearing is the only gift you have left to give—and that’s a very lonely, very convincing lie that your pain is telling you. But kindness isn’t measured by your absence; it’s measured by the moments you stay, even when staying is messy and hard and imperfect. Your kids won’t remember a perfect father—they’ll remember one who chose to be there, who let them see that struggle doesn’t mean the end. Please, before you make any permanent decision, give yourself one hour to call or text a crisis line—988 in the U.S.—and let someone sit with you in this exact moment. You don’t have to be the one to hold every weight alone.",
